# Michael Arnaldi

Dependency injection supplies service implementations to callers.
Resource safety means cleaning up resources after use. Concurrency control manages work that runs at the same time.

Michael traces Effect to a TypeScript team's needs for dependency injection, reliable tests, resource safety, concurrency control, and retries. [Effect Days 2024, 08:40](https://youtu.be/7sJc3Z4mh1w?t=520).

He describes Effect computations through their outputs, predictable failures, and requirements: the services the work needs. [Happy Path 81, 49:15](https://youtu.be/gc5P36t6kD0?t=2955).
